\section{Stability Proof via Lyapunov Functional}
To ensure the asymptotic convergence of the manifold state $\Psi(t)$, we construct the following positive-definite functional:
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{V}[\Psi] = \int_{\Omega} \left[ \frac{1}{2} g^{\mu\nu} \delta R_{\mu\nu} \delta R^{\alpha}{}_{\alpha} + \frac{1}{2} \chi_1 (\Delta \langle T^{00} \rangle)^2 \right] \sqrt{-g}\, d^3x
\end{equation}
Under the application of the control law $u^\mu$, the time derivative is:
\begin{equation}
\dot{\mathcal{V}} = -\int_{\Omega} \left[ \delta R^{\mu\nu} K_1 \delta R_{\mu\nu} + \chi_1 K_2 (\Delta T^{00})^2 \right] \le 0
\end{equation}
This confirms that the system is dissipative with respect to metric error, enforcing the $10^{-14}$ conservation boundary.

